        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00038">Compare your answer:</para>
              <media alt="">
              <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_10_07_06_04.jpg"/>
            </media>
          
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="e91e1f89-ee24-4fd8-a748-9709bcd4de75" class="multiple-choice">
        <problem id="prob-00009">
          <para id="para-00039">Are the solutions you found using the two methods close?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00009">
          <para id="para-00040">Correct! Yes. Solutions were the same: \(x \approx -4.949\) and \(x \approx -0.051\).</para>
          <para id="para-00041">Incorrect. The correct answer is Yes. \(x \approx -4.949\) and \(x \approx -0.051\).</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <exercise id="exer-00007">
        <problem id="prob-00010">
          <para id="para-00042">\(x^2+\frac{8}{3}x+\frac{14}{9}=0\)</para>
          <para id="para-00043">Find the exact solutions by completing the square.</para>
          <para id="para-00044">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00010">
          <para id="para-00045">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00046">\(\begin{array}{rcl} x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\frac{14}{9} &amp;=&amp;0 \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\left(\frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{8}{3}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9}+\left(\frac{1}{2} \cdot \frac{8}{3}\right)^{2} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9}+\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\frac{16}{9} &amp;=&amp;-\frac{14}{9}+\frac{16}{9} \\ x^{2}+\frac{8}{3} x+\frac{16}{9} &amp;=&amp;\frac{2}{9} \\ \left(x+\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2} &amp;=&amp;\frac{2}{9} \\ \sqrt{\left(x+\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2}} &amp;=&amp;\sqrt{\frac{2}{9}} \\ x+\frac{4}{3} &amp;=&amp;\pm \frac{\sqrt{2}}{3} \\ x &amp;=&amp;-\frac{4}{3} \pm \frac{\sqrt{2}}{3} \end{array}\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00004">
        <item>Graph the equation to find approximate solutions.</item>
